# Fresh Coders 2.0 — Euphoria 2026 : Netlify environment variables

Copy the variables below into Netlify (Site configuration → Environment variables)
and the backend host (Render / Railway / Fly.io / VPS – see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).

## On NETLIFY (frontend build)
These are read at build time (Vite inlines `VITE_*` into the bundle).

| Variable                 | Value / example                                  | Notes                                              |
|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| `VITE_API_BASE_URL`      | *(empty)*                                        | Empty = demo mode (in-browser backend, no server). |
| `VITE_API_BASE_URL`      | `https://fresh-coders-api.onrender.com`          | Set this once the Flask API is hosted to use the real backend. |

`NODE_VERSION` is already set to `20` via `netlify.toml`.

## On the BACKEND HOST (Flask API) — not Netlify
Netlify does not run Python. Host `src/backend` on any Python host and set:

| Variable           | Value / example                                               | Required |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|----------|
| `SECRET_KEY`       | long random string (see below)                                | yes      |
| `FLASK_ENV`        | `production`                                                  | yes      |
| `CORS_ORIGINS`     | comma-separated site URLs, e.g. `https://your-site.netlify.app` | yes      |
| `TURSO_DB_URL`     | `libsql://fresh-coder-euphoria-at-kare-university-2026-vvsrinath0.aws-ap-south-1.turso.io` | yes |
| `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN` | DB-scoped token minted for that database                      | yes      |
| `DATABASE_PATH`    | `database/fresh_coders.sqlite` (default)                     | no       |
| `SESSION_TTL_HOURS`| `8`                                                          | no       |

Copy `src/backend/.env.example` → `src/backend/.env` on the backend host and
fill the values. Tests stay on the local SQLite file automatically.

## Local, real secrets (NOT committed)
`.env.netlify` in this repo contains the actual values (Turso DB token, SECRET_KEY,
Netlify URL placeholders). It is gitignored – it exists so you can copy-paste the
real values into the Netlify/Render dashboards. Never commit it.